urodegenerative disorders. In the presence of ACMSD, ACMS is converted to AMS, a benign catabolite (PubMed:12140278). ACMSD ultimately controls the metabolic fate of tryptophan catabolism along the kynurenine pathway (PubMed:12140278, PubMed:19843166)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}